{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Upon his hand, a second time, saying.</b> That is, a spark of ruach ha-kodesh flashed in the midwife and she acted without knowing what she did. She tied upon his hand a second time, and this alludes that he is second, not first, but she said, ״זֶה יָצָא רִאשׁוֹנָה״. And this is the verse's saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> ״זֶה יָצָא רִאשׁוֹנָה״ — meaning, she said thus, but according to the truth the sign indicates the opposite, for there is a mother to the tradition."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:56.105016218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}